dance":[2,1,1,1.71,{"raise":0,"reaffirm":0,"cut":2}],"ai_disruption":[0,0,0,0.0]},"move":{"r1":0.1516,"r5":0.2847,"r1_spy":0.1555,"r5_spy":0.2919}}],"quotes":[{"c":"BOOT 2019 Q3","e":"boot","d":"2019-02-05","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Gregory V. Hackman","x":"We have increased our full year guidance and now expect same-store sales growth to be approximately 10%.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/02/06/boot-barn-holdings-inc-boot-q3-2019-earnings-confe.aspx"},{"c":"BOOT 2019 Q4","e":"boot","d":"2019-05-16","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"James G. Conroy","x":"Before I turn the call over to Greg, I'd like to provide some commentary on tariffs, certainly a topical subject at the moment.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/05/16/boot-barn-holdings-inc-boot-q4-2019-earnings-call.aspx"},{"c":"BOOT 2019 Q4","e":"boot","d":"2019-05-16","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"James G. Conroy","x":"We would expect that our vendors and their factories would absorb at least a portion of any additional tariffs.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/05/16/boot-barn-holdings-inc-boot-q4-2019-earnings-call.aspx"},{"c":"BOOT 2019 Q4","e":"boot","d":"2019-05-16","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"James G. Conroy","x":"Having said that, given the functional and somewhat non-discretionary nature of much of our business, we believe that we could pass along modest price increases for most of our categories to cover any incremental costs passed to us from our vendor partners.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/05/16/boot-barn-holdings-inc-boot-q4-2019-earnings-call.aspx"},{"c":"BOOT 2020 Q1","e":"boot","d":"2019-07-31","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Greg Hackman","x":"So we're raising our guidance mainly based on the Q1 beat with also folding in the change in the revolver balance and paying down the term loan and we did bump our Q2 same-store sales expectation a bit.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/08/01/boot-barn-holdings-inc-boot-q1-2020-earnings-call.aspx"},{"c":"BOOT 2020 Q2","e":"boot","d":"2019-10-30","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"James G. Conroy","x":"…acceleration of our exclusive brand business, coupled with an expansion in our initial markup structure due to our purchasing power our exclusive brand merchandise will over-deliver our planned margin contribution for the business, despite the impact of new tariffs on the China sourced goods.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/10/31/boot-barn-holdings-inc-boot-q2-2020-earnings-call.aspx"},{"c":"BOOT 2020 Q2","e":"boot","d":"2019-10-30","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Gregory V. Hackman","x":"At this point, I'd like to provide you with an update on tariffs.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/10/31/boot-barn-holdings-inc-boot-q2-2020-earnings-call.aspx"},{"c":"BOOT 2020 Q2","e":"boot","d":"2019-10-30","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Gregory V. Hackman","x":"Two of our top 5 vendors have informed us that they are continuing to evaluate the situation but that there will not be a price increase until February 1, 2020 at the earliest.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/10/31/boot-barn-holdings-inc-boot-q2-2020-earnings-call.aspx"},{"c":"BOOT 2020 Q2","e":"boot","d":"2019-10-30","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"James G. Conroy","x":"If we do look at what happened to the List 3 items which are small leather goods, belts to handbags, they initially didn't take price there as well, and then they did pass on price increases.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/10/31/boot-barn-holdings-inc-boot-q2-2020-earnings-call.aspx"},{"c":"BOOT 2020 Q2","e":"boot","d":"2019-10-30","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"James G. Conroy","x":"From a store operations perspective we see continued benefit from the streamlining of certain administrative tasks in our stores giving our floor team the opportunity to focus more of their time on driving improved sales results through enhanced service and selling initiatives.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/10/31/boot-barn-holdings-inc-boot-q2-2020-earnings-call.aspx"},{"c":"BOOT 2020 Q3","e":"boot","d":"2020-02-04","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Gregory V. Hackman","x":"But we haven't seen sort of massive layoffs or any real disruption and employment in oil patch.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/02/05/boot-barn-holdings-inc-boot-q3-2020-earnings-call.aspx"},{"c":"BOOT 2020 Q3","e":"boot","d":"2020-02-04","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"James G. Conroy","x":"So we -- and to your point, there are people that unfortunately are closing their stores and making real estate available in some cases in the right size and shape that we need.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/02/05/boot-barn-holdings-inc-boot-q3-2020-earnings-call.aspx"},{"c":"BOOT 2020 Q4","e":"boot","d":"2020-05-20","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"James G. Conroy","x":"At Boot Barn and perhaps many other retailers like us, the tariff saber rattling created a lot of that flexibility over the last year or so.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/05/20/boot-barn-holdings-inc-boot-q4-2020-earnings-call.aspx"},{"c":"BOOT 2021 Q1","e":"boot","d":"2020-08-04","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"James Conroy","x":"These measures included pay cuts for management, reduced store hours, corporatewide furloughs and layoffs, reductions in marketing spend and the minimization of third-party expenses.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/08/05/boot-barn-holdings-inc-boot-q1-2021-earnings-call.aspx"},{"c":"BOOT 2021 Q2","e":"boot","d":"2020-10-28","l":"streaming","r":"management","s":"James G. Conroy","x":"We believe these enhancements provide us with additional competitive advantage, including same-day delivery of holiday gifts purchased on our sites, which will extend our online shopping season several days longer than traditional direct-to-consumer players.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/10/29/boot-barn-holdings-inc-boot-q2-2021-earnings-call/"},{"c":"BOOT 2021 Q2","e":"boot","d":"2020-10-28","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"James G. Conroy","x":"The strong full price selling, combined with our recent cost reduction efforts, resulted in second quarter net income of $5.8 million or $0.20 per diluted share.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/10/29/boot-barn-holdings-inc-boot-q2-2021-earnings-call/"},{"c":"BOOT 2021 Q3","e":"boot","d":"2021-01-25","l":"streaming","r":"management","s":"James G. Conroy","x":"We were encouraged by the effectiveness of our direct-to-consumer supply chain which was able to meet outsized customer demand, while avoiding virtually all anticipated issues with package delivery service.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/01/25/boot-barn-holdings-inc-boot-q3-2021-earnings-call/"},{"c":"BOOT 2021 Q3","e":"boot","d":"2021-01-25","l":"streaming","r":"management","s":"James G. Conroy","x":"…out UPS surcharges and issues of getting the product delivered and we need some gratitude going through the supply chain and the folks in which they kind of run the direct to consumer fulfillment, but we were able to avoid a big uptick in the freight charges and most of it happen going forward.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/01/25/boot-barn-holdings-inc-boot-q3-2021-earnings-call/"},{"c":"BOOT 2021 Q3","e":"boot","d":"2021-01-25","l":"pricing_power","r":"analyst","s":"Matthew R. Boss","x":"On your comments around continued margin strength in January, could you just elaborate on drivers of pricing power that you see from a merchandise margin perspective and any impediments to driving similar or greater merchandise margin expansion in the fourth quarter?","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/01/25/boot-barn-holdings-inc-boot-q3-2021-earnings-call/"},{"c":"BOOT 2021 Q4","e":"boot","d":"2021-05-12","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Greg Hackman","x":"And so I think we'll be able to again manage our margin rate at the level we've done in the past, even with those price increases.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/05/12/boot-barn-holdings-inc-boot-q4-2021-earnings-call/"},{"c":"BOOT 2022 Q1","e":"boot","d":"2021-08-04","l":"theater","r":"analyst","s":"Peter Keith","x":"Hey, good afternoon, Bobby premier on for theater, messenger says, looks like a pretty large infrastructure bill, getting close to be passed in Congress wonder if you could discuss how previous infrastructure programs have impacted demand trends and know what you might expect this time around?","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/08/04/boot-barn-holdings-inc-boot-q2-2021-earnings-call/"},{"c":"BOOT 2022 Q1","e":"boot","d":"2021-08-04","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Greg Hackman","x":"Stevens, it's Greg, we have seen a handful of our vendors raise price in the first quarter.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/08/04/boot-barn-holdings-inc-boot-q2-2021-earnings-call/"},{"c":"BOOT 2022 Q1","e":"boot","d":"2021-08-04","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Greg Hackman","x":"And as you just described, we we passed that price increase along for the customer with our normal markup, right.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/08/04/boot-barn-holdings-inc-boot-q2-2021-earnings-call/"},{"c":"BOOT 2022 Q2","e":"boot","d":"2021-10-27","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"James G. Conroy","x":"And some of them also were passing through freight expenses or freight charges that were more than what our exclusive brands was experiencing.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/10/28/boot-barn-holdings-inc-boot-q2-2022-earnings-call/"},{"c":"BOOT 2022 Q2","e":"boot","d":"2021-10-27","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"James G. Conroy","x":"So I think most of the industry passes along price increase.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/10/28/boot-barn-holdings-inc-boot-q2-2022-earnings-call/"},{"c":"BOOT 2026 Q3","e":"boot","d":"2026-02-04","l":"dtc","r":"analyst","s":"Max Rakhlenko","x":"And specifically, any comments on the farm and ranch channel and separately DTC as of your vendors are going more direct?","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/02/04/boot-barn-boot-q3-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"BOOT 2026 Q3","e":"boot","d":"2026-02-04","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"John Hazen","x":"Our team has continued to diligently work with our factory partners to mitigate the impact of tariffs through cost concessions, which have allowed us to maintain pricing on some goods.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/02/04/boot-barn-boot-q3-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"BOOT 2026 Q3","e":"boot","d":"2026-02-04","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"John Hazen","x":"We had some a lot of fluid activity with tariffs and bringing product in sooner and later.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/02/04/boot-barn-boot-q3-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"BOOT 2026 Q3","e":"boot","d":"2026-02-04","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"John Hazen","x":"We knew I knew we were going to take price increases.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/02/04/boot-barn-boot-q3-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"BOOT 2026 Q3","e":"boot","d":"2026-02-04","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"John Hazen","x":"And looking at where we can take a price increase that covers the margin rate for product or maybe a little bit more if we decide to hold on another particular product.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/02/04/boot-barn-boot-q3-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"BOOT 2026 Q3","e":"boot","d":"2026-02-04","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Jim Watkins","x":"Based on our year-to-date performance and fourth quarter outlook, we are raising our full-year guidance.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/02/04/boot-barn-boot-q3-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"BOOT 2026 Q4","e":"boot","d":"2026-05-14","l":"streaming","r":"management","s":"John Hazen","x":"I spent 2 days, 1 day at our stores at stores, 1 day at the event, and 1 day watching the streaming side of it, which I -- was the part that I was most excited about.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/05/15/boot-barn-boot-q4-2026-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"BOOT 2026 Q4","e":"boot","d":"2026-05-14","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"John Hazen","x":"As the tariff landscape evolved, the team's mitigation efforts and factory negotiations helped drive margin expansion over the past year.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/05/15/boot-barn-boot-q4-2026-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"BOOT 2026 Q4","e":"boot","d":"2026-05-14","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Jim Watkins","x":"Additionally, our outlook excludes the potential recovery of approximately $18 million in IEEPA tariff refund that we are actively pursuing.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/05/15/boot-barn-boot-q4-2026-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"BOOT 2026 Q4","e":"boot","d":"2026-05-14","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Jim Watkins","x":"And then we will adapt to whatever tariff environment comes at us similar to what we did last year, if we need to raise prices because we're seeing price increases, and that's something we'll do.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/05/15/boot-barn-boot-q4-2026-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"BOOT 2026 Q4","e":"boot","d":"2026-05-14","l":"pricing_power","r":"analyst","s":"Maksim Rakhlenko","x":"